            "\n",
            "Imagine standing before a majestic tree, its branches stretchi...\n",
            "----------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "\n",
            "🔬 SCIENCE Expert:\n",
            "Recursion is a fundamental concept in computer science and mathematics that can be a bit tricky to grasp at first, but don't worry, I'll break it down in a way that's easy to understand.\n",
            "\n",
            "**What is Recursion?**\n",
            "\n",
            "Recursion is a problem-solving technique where a function or method calls itself repeate...\n",
            "----------------------------------------------------------------------\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# ---- Demonstrating Expert Specialization: Same query, different experts ----\n",
        "# This shows WHY routing matters — the same question gets very different answers\n",
        "# depending on which \"expert\" handles it.\n",
        "\n",
        "query = \"Explain recursion.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Query: '{query}'\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
        "for expert_key in [\"code\", \"creative\", \"science\"]:\n",
        "    chain  = build_expert_chain(expert_key)\n",
        "    answer = chain.invoke({\"query\": query})\n",
        "    emoji  = EXPERTS[expert_key][\"emoji\"]\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n{emoji} {expert_key.upper()} Expert:\")\n",
        "    print(answer[:300] + \"...\" if len(answer) > 300 else answer)\n",
        "    print(\"-\" * 70)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "b0c1d2e3",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b0c1d2e3"
      },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Summary\n",
        "\n",
        "### Generation Enhancement — Full Picture\n",
        "\n",
        "| Technique | What It Does | When to Use | Key Library |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| **Full Fine-Tuning** | Updates all weights | Large budget, very specialized domain | `transformers`, `Trainer` |\n",
        "| **LoRA / PEFT** | Trains tiny adapter matrices (< 1% of params) | Medium budget, task adaptation | `peft` |\n",
        "| **FP16 / BF16** | Half-precision training/inference | Always — halves memory, negligible quality loss | `torch.float16` |\n",
        "| **INT8 Quantization** | 8-bit weights (4x memory reduction) | Inference on consumer hardware | `bitsandbytes` |\n",
        "| **INT4 / GPTQ** | 4-bit weights (8x memory reduction) | Running 70B models on a single GPU | `bitsandbytes`, `auto-gptq` |\n",
        "| **Software MoE** | Routes queries to specialist prompts | Multi-domain chatbots, enterprise assistants | LangChain |\n",
        "| **Model MoE** | Sparse expert activation per token | Best quality-per-FLOP at scale | Mixtral, GPT-4 |\n",
        "\n",
        "### LoRA Key Formula\n",
        "$$W' = W + \\Delta W = W + BA \\quad \\text{where } B \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d \\times r}, A \\in \\mathbb{R}^{r \\times d}, r \\ll d$$\n",
        "\n",
        "### Quantization Key Formula\n",
        "$$x_{\\text{INT8}} = \\text{round}\\left(\\frac{x}{S}\\right) + Z, \\quad S = \\frac{x_{\\max} - x_{\\min}}{255}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "### MoE Key Concept\n",
        "$$\\text{output} = \\sum_{i \\in \\text{Top-K}} G(x)_i \\cdot E_i(x)$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Where $G(x)$ is the router's gating probability and $E_i(x)$ is the output of expert $i$.\n",
        "\n",
        "**You have now completed Unit 3!** The full progression:\n",
        "- **Notebook 1**: Better retrieval (BM25, SBERT, ColBERT, Hybrid + RRF)\n",
        "- **Notebook 2**: Better candidates (Re-Ranking, HyDE, Multi-Query)\n",
        "- **Notebook 3**: Better generation (Fine-Tuning, Quantization, MoE)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Key Learnings — Generation Enhancement (Unit 3, Notebook 3)\n",
        "\n",
        "### When to Use What\n",
        "- Need new FACTS → RAG | Need new STYLE/BEHAVIOR → Fine-Tune | Simple fix → Prompt Engineering\n",
        "\n",
        "### LoRA\n",
        "- Freezes original W, trains only 2 tiny matrices: **W' = W + B·A**\n",
        "- Rank r=4 on 64×64 matrix → only 512 params trained (12.5%) instead of 4096\n",
        "- B initialized to zero → at start, LoRA output = base model output\n",
        "- Save only the tiny adapter after training, not the whole model\n",
        "\n",
        "### Precision\n",
        "- FP16 overflows at 65504 → 70000 becomes `inf` ← dangerous\n",
        "- BF16 same memory as FP16 but same range as FP32 → preferred for LLMs\n",
        "- 1B param model: FP32=3.73GB, FP16=1.86GB, INT8=0.93GB, INT4=0.47GB\n",
        "\n",
        "### Quantization\n",
        "- Formula: `x_INT8 = round(x/S) + Z` where S=scale, Z=zero point\n",
        "- INT8 = sweet spot → 4x compression, max error only 0.003\n",
        "- INT4 = 8x compression, still usable | INT2 = too lossy, not practical\n",
        "- Llama-3.1-8B: 29.8GB FP32 → 3.73GB INT4 (fits on laptop GPU!)\n",
        "\n",
        "### MoE\n",
        "- Dense models activate ALL params per token — wasteful\n",
        "- MoE router picks top-2 experts per token, rest stay idle\n",
        "- Mixtral 8x7B: 47B total but only 13B active → speed of 13B, knowledge of 47B\n",
        "- Router must use temperature=0.0 for deterministic classification\n",
        "- Same query \"Explain recursion\" → CODE gave Python, CREATIVE used tree metaphor, SCIENCE used headers/definitions\n",
        "- Router got 5/5 correct in the notebook demo"
      ],
      "metadata": {
